# Authors

## Talaria

- **Mike-Jeason Leca** — product design, tool surface, sandbox and signing pipeline,
  audit rules, this packaging.
- **the earlier prototype's author** — original `hermes-shortcuts-builder`, the source-first product
  contract, the alert-template baseline this work grew from.

## Upstream lineage

Talaria is derived from [`an earlier internal prototype`](an earlier internal prototype)
(MIT). The original three-tool surface and its "the model writes the source, the tool
does not" contract are the earlier author's. Everything Talaria adds — sandboxed compilation, artifact
library, AEA1 decoding, signing consent, action corpus, audit pass — is new here.

## Third-party

Cherri (https://github.com/electrikmilk/cherri) is invoked as a separate process and is
not linked into or redistributed with this plugin. Its own licence (GPL-2.0) governs that
binary. Apple, iOS and Shortcuts are trademarks of Apple Inc.; this project is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Apple.
